text:
marta: customer reports edge TypeScript streaming hangs after auth retry, looks like only first chunk arrives then nothing. logs attached below.

raj: can you paste quick repro + sdk version?

marta: repro steps:
1) install @redwood/inference@0.10.0 on a Node edge-like runtime
2) run this handler in a dev edge sim
```
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.KEY });
export default async function handler(req) {
  const res = await client.stream({ model: 'gpt-test', input: 'hello' });
  const reader = res.body.getReader();
  let done = false;
  while (!done) {
    const { value, done: d } = await reader.read();
    done = d;
    if (value) console.log('chunk', new TextDecoder().decode(value));
  }
}
```
Observed behavior: prints first chunk, then stream stalls. Network trace shows an auth refresh (+401) and then a retry, after which the ReadableStream appears locked/closed.

leo: paste from runtime logs:
```
[edge-runtime] 2024-05-12T14:03:21Z auth: refresh started
[edge-runtime] 2024-05-12T14:03:21Z request: chunk 1 sent
[edge-runtime] 2024-05-12T14:03:22Z auth: refresh complete
[edge-runtime] 2024-05-12T14:03:22Z fetch: retry attempt 1 for /v1/stream
[edge-runtime] 2024-05-12T14:03:23Z stream: reader.locked? true
Error: TypeError: Failed to execute 'getReader' on 'ReadableStream': The stream is locked.
```

raj: this matches a race we fixed in later client builds — the retry logic can call fetch() again while user code still holds a reader, leaving the web stream in a locked / closed state when the second connection replaces the first. i can repro on local edge sim with @redwood/inference@0.10.0, cannot repro with 0.10.2.

marta: customer is on 0.10.0, traffic impacted since 2024-05-12, high priority. they see intermittent 401 then never resume. :frowning:

leo: temporary mitigations:
- pin SDK to 0.10.2+ OR
- set env REDWOOD_STREAM_RETRY=0 to disable automatic retry on auth in edge until patch
Both stop the hang for our repro.

support-bot: Created ticket SUP-1298 and assigned to @raj for patch + rollout. Escalation: please notify eng-runtime if >100 qps affected.

raj: i'll open a tracking PR, include a small canary (dedicated pool + 20% traffic) and a backwards-compatible guard to avoid double-acquiring reader. planning patch 0.10.3 with regression test.

marta: thanks team — i'll update the customer with workaround (pin to 0.10.2) and share the repro snippet.
